From: Teoman Madran <teoman@madran.me>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: wait for the chip to settle after reset

rtl8365mb_reset_chip() returns as soon as the HW reset bit self-clears,
but the chip keeps loading its internal defaults after that. On an
RTL8367S (ver 0x00A0) behind an IPQ5018 this intermittently left CPU
port traffic forwarded to no user port after a cold boot, until the
driver was rebound.

Realtek documents about 1 s for the chip to come out of reset, and the
vendor driver waits 500 ms after the reset and again after init. Wait
1 s after the reset before configuring the chip. With this, 10/10 cold
boots plus warm and button reboots came up with working forwarding.

Signed-off-by: Teoman Madran <teoman@madran.me>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -3046,6 +3046,11 @@ static int rtl8365mb_setup(struct dsa_sw
 		goto out_error;
 	}
 
+	/* The reset bit clears before the chip has finished loading its
+	 * defaults. Realtek documents about 1 s for the chip to come up.
+	 */
+	msleep(1000);
+
 	ret = rtl8365mb_sds_probe_option(priv);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(priv->dev, "failed to reset chip: %pe\n",
